#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110351 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/id #uuid "30974188-c734-5e99-a9ae-81d1a53b9105" :question/math-academy-id "e-14854" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched below.\n\n![](images/e5/e5393f15ff154f1f4cc310791790db0fe0ad0d9faa076d10f3f6ec7b481de086.png)" :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are $x_1=-3$ and $x_2=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{-3+2}{2}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\dfrac{1}{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110352 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/id #uuid "00575d99-28e6-59b7-b416-765808916fe5" :question/math-academy-id "e-14857" :question/problem "Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=-(x-1)(x-5).$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=-(x-1)(x-5),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=1$ and $x_2=5.$\n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\nx = \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2} = \\dfrac{1+5}{2} = 3\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110353 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/id #uuid "405e0230-69cb-5679-bec0-13a69c722934" :question/math-academy-id "e-14860" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2)$ is $x=6.$ Find the value of $k.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we will calculate the axis of symmetry in terms of $k.$ Then, since we know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6,$ we will set our result equal to $6.$ \n\nFrom the equation $y=\\dfrac14(x-k)(x+2),$ we find that the roots of the parabola are $x_1=k$ and $x_2=-2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{k-2}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe know that the axis of symmetry is $x=6.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{k-2}{2} & =6 \\\\ k-2 & =12 \\\\ k & =14.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110373 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110728 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9a2eed2b-7f94-5b53-bc5c-4bf9aea18d32" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Vertex of a Parabola From Table Data"}] :question/id #uuid "04877936-271e-5fcb-a1ea-aa39c52482b6" :question/math-academy-id "e-19740" :question/problem "| **$x$** | $4$ | $12$ | $20$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **$f(x)$** | $9$ | $25$ | $9$ |\n\nThe graph of a parabola $y = f(x)$ passes through the points given by their $(x,y)$-coordinates in the table above. What is the $x$-coordinate of the parabola's vertex?" :question/worked-solution "Notice that the values of $f(x)$ at the points $x=4$ and $x=20$ are equal.\n\n$$\nf(4) = f(20) = 9\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola's axis of symmetry must be equidistant from the lines $x=4$ and $x=20.$ We can find this by taking the average of these two values.\n\nIf the parabolas vertex is $(h,k),$ then we must have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}h & =\\frac{4+20}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186541059 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} {:answer/id #uuid "62de6123-6a95-5dae-88e9-843c5a0c968d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540695} {:answer/id #uuid "cac0d315-ce7f-5d80-9e6a-46b1ae01e841" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540866} {:answer/id #uuid "dc0cfaa1-d45c-5039-a04f-63b0fdededc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-2.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540902} {:answer/id #uuid "e784cab5-862c-5407-ae59-9868332a3944" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e9f3df9-da61-5f4a-b3ab-8a1a1cda444a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x=-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540607} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba3ac59-9466-58f5-9b5b-efe7c90f5528" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "094a6192-1567-5375-9e5c-b0ab7210d2c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-106137" :question/problem "![](images/e1/e1fdcc8a8ed9dd9936ade0b088a672eadea1ca9ae7b12de7ce1b1dead2c3014a.png)\n\nFind the axis of symmetry for the parabola sketched above." :question/worked-solution "From the graph, we deduce that the roots are ${x}_{1}=-4$ and ${x}_{2}=2.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2}=\\frac{(-4)+2}{2}=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-1.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110976 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "42832b65-324f-56f7-9cbe-c9bf43389fde" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the X-Intercepts"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47acc35f-5b61-5d14-8bcc-66ac1ea76bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{30}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540654} :answer-field/id #uuid "caf9ab22-db76-5d02-b2ce-c710382a7b35" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107604}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5f8c9da4-4b17-554e-b183-7584d639d444" :question/math-academy-id "q-223659" :question/problem "![](images/3b/3b0ebd3a9a282fca4dc4302549c22efe674ada772eb00ed5e8aa0abbe275074b.png)\n\nThe graph above shows a parabola. The $x$-coordinates of $A$ and $B$ are $-\\frac{8}{3}$ and $\\frac{11}{5},$ respectively.  Find the axis of symmetry of the parabola.\n\nThe axis of symmetry is $x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We're given that the roots of the parabola are \n ${x}_{1}=-\\frac{8}{3}$ and ${x}_{2}=\\frac{11}{5}.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{8}{3}+\\frac{11}{5})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{40}{15}+\\frac{33}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\frac{7}{15})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{30}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=-\\frac{7}{30}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555793 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110726 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "23f4cc44-569e-56bd-aaa6-b72a10970679" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Axis of Symmetry From the Parabola’s Equation in Factored Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fb5a3b2-6779-5f18-aee9-35c71d01843c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7fb5a3b2-6779-5f18-aee9-35c71d01843c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555296} :answer-field/id #uuid "ff2d3b83-418c-57aa-abbd-ad23104f3a79" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555757}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3c9a4b7b-8e3b-5aa3-8825-873abec27dfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-223666" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y=(x-1)(x-9)$ is $x=${{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the equation $y=(x-1)(x-9),$ we can tell that the roots of the parabola are ${x}_{1}=1$ and ${x}_{2}=9.$ \n\nTo find the axis of symmetry, we take the average of the roots, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+9}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the axis of symmetry is $x=5.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110978 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110727 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89428829-1c13-5c7e-9fc2-ffe526a4c33a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding an Unknown Value Given the Axis of Symmetry"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "9fc6a2b7-5d2f-5c82-ae12-de24bf2f6659" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186107606}] :question/id #uuid "8660b4e2-d758-5150-9ae4-48bf3487cb6a" :question/math-academy-id "q-223695" :question/problem "The axis of symmetry of the parabola $y = - (x + 5k)(3x - 4k)$ is $x =-\\frac{1}{8}$. Find the value of $k$.$k =$\n{{field-1}}"}]}
